;; M4S recursive construction self-join (docs/m4s-contract.md, required
;; fixtures): closure by self-join where every closure row is a CONSTRUCTED
;; struct term -- the struct analog of m4t_selfjoin.  With the 3-cycle
;; r0(1,2), r0(2,3), r0(3,1) the closure is all nine pairs over {1,2,3}:
;;   sr (2,1) -> (input 0, nonrec 0, rec 3)   (2,Y)+(Y,1) for Y in {1,2,3}
;; and sedge interns nine contents with the same support words.
;;
;; Cutting the cycle (delete r0(1,2)) leaves the closure of
;; { (2,3), (3,1) } = { (2,3), (3,1), (2,1) }:
;;   sr (2,3) -> (0, 1, 0)    copy of r0(2,3)
;;   sr (3,1) -> (0, 1, 0)    copy of r0(3,1)
;;   sr (2,1) -> (0, 0, 1)    (2,3)+(3,1) only
;; so sedge holds 3 live ids and 6 tombstones after settlement.

table (r0 int int)
struct (sedge int int)
table (sr sedge)

rule
(r0 X Y)
-->
(sr (sedge X Y))

rule
(sr (sedge X Y))
(sr (sedge Y Z))
-->
(sr (sedge X Z))
